  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "At a party, each person shakes hands with exactly 3 other people. If fewer than 75 handshakes take place, then what is the maximum number of people at the party?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "48 people.\n\nCount each handshake twice; the number of people must be even and less than 50.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the number of people and $H$ the number of handshakes. Counting three handshakes per person counts each handshake twice.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}H&=\\frac{3n}{2}\\\\\\frac{3n}{2}&<75\\\\n&<50\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $3n=2H$, $n$ must be even. The greatest even integer below 50 is 48.\n\nThis is possible: arrange the 48 people into 12 groups of four, with everyone shaking hands with the other three people in their group. This gives $12\\times6=72$ handshakes.\n\nThe maximum is 48 people.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 42
  },
